# Dispatcher

- Filters are an allow-list (ADR-015). Deny everything first, then allow exact paths, extensions and selectors. Don't include `default_filters.any`.
- A new public endpoint needs three things in the same PR: a filter rule, a cache rule, and a TTL that matches SD-08 in `SOLUTION_DESIGN.md`.
- Persisted queries: allow `GET /graphql/execute.json/airline/*` only. Never allow `/graphql/execute.json` without the configuration name, or `POST /content/cq:graphql/*`.
- Cache lifetimes come from AEM headers (`HtmlCacheHeadersFilter`, persisted-query `cache-control` and `surrogate-control`). Don't hard-code TTLs in `.any` files unless the design says so.
- Files marked immutable by the Dispatcher SDK must not be edited. Change the `*.farm` or `*.vhost` files in `enabled_*` and `available_*` only.
- Run `bin/validate.sh src` (Dispatcher SDK) before opening a PR. If you can't, say so in the PR (see README departures).
- AI-generated Dispatcher changes are reviewed with `.ai/prompts/dispatcher-review.md` and by a human. Treat them as security changes.
